  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8203;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>​&nbsp;is an example of freon. It can act as an aerosol propellant, refrigerant, or organic solvent because it is&nbsp;a gas at room temperature and a liquid when cooled or compressed. Freon is a term that was commonly used to refer to a group of chlorofluorocarbon (CFC) and hydrochlorofluorocarbon (HCFC) compounds.</p>",
